.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_STORE_set_verify_cb
sets the verification callback of
.Fa xs
to
.Fa verify_cb
overwriting the previous callback.
The callback assigned with this function becomes a default for the one
that can be assigned directly to the corresponding
.Vt X509_STORE_CTX ,
please see
.Xr X509_STORE_CTX_set_verify_cb 3
for further information.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_verify
sets the final chain verification function for
.Fa xs
to
.Fa verify .
Its purpose is to go through the chain of certificates and check that
all signatures are valid and that the current time is within the limits
of each certificate's first and last validity time.
The final chain verification functions must return 0 on failure and 1 on
success.
.Em \&If no chain verification function is provided, the internal default function will be used instead.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_CTX_get1_issuer
tries to find a certificate from the
.Em store
component of
.Fa ctx
that has a subject name matching the issuer name of
.Fa x
and is accepted by the
.Fa check_issued
function in
.Fa ctx .
On success it assigns to
.Em *issuer
the first match that has a suitable validity period or otherwise has the
latest expiration date of all matching certificates.
If the function returns 1 the caller is responsible for freeing
.Em *issuer .
Note that this search does not support backtracking.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_get_issuer
sets the function
.Fa get_issuer
that is used to get the "best" candidate issuer certificate of the given
certificate
.Fa x .
When such a certificate is found,
.Fa get_issuer
must up-ref and assign it to
.Em *issuer
and then return 1. Otherwise
.Fa get_issuer
must return 0 if not found and -1 (or 0) on failure.
If
.Fn X509_STORE_set_get_issuer
is not used or
.Fa get_issuer
is NULL then
.Fn X509_STORE_CTX_get1_issuer
is used as the default implementation.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_check_issued
sets the function to check that a given certificate
.Fa x
is issued by the issuer certificate
.Fa issuer .
This function must return 0 on failure (among others if
.Fa x
hasn't been issued with
.Fa issuer )
and 1 on success.
.Em \&If no function to get the issuer is provided, the internal default function will be used instead.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_check_revocation
sets the revocation checking function.
Its purpose is to look through the final chain and check the revocation
status for each certificate.
It must return 0 on failure and 1 on success.
.Em \&If no function to get the issuer is provided, the internal default function will be used instead.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_get_crl
sets the function to get the crl for a given certificate
.Fa x .
When found, the crl must be assigned to
.Em *crl .
This function must return 0 on failure and 1 on success.
.Em \&If no function to get the issuer is provided, the internal default function will be used instead.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_check_crl
sets the function to check the validity of the given
.Em crl .
This function must return 0 on failure and 1 on success.
.Em \&If no function to get the issuer is provided, the internal default function will be used instead.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_cert_crl
sets the function to check the revocation status of the given
certificate
.Fa x
against the given
.Em crl .
This function must return 0 on failure and 1 on success.
.Em \&If no function to get the issuer is provided, the internal default function will be used instead.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_check_policy
sets the function to check the policies of all the certificates in the
final chain..
This function must return 0 on failure and 1 on success.
.Em \&If no function to get the issuer is provided, the internal default function will be used instead.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_lookup_certs
and
.Fn X509_STORE_set_lookup_crls
set the functions to look up all the certs or all the CRLs that match
the given name
.Em nm .
These functions return NULL on failure and a pointer to a stack of
certificates
.Pf ( Vt X509 )
or to a stack of CRLs
.Pf ( Sy X509_CRL )
on success.
.Em \&If no function to get the issuer is provided, the internal default function will be used instead.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_cleanup
sets the final cleanup function, which is called when the context
.Pf ( Vt X509_STORE_CTX )
is being torn down.
This function doesn't return any value.
.Em \&If no function to get the issuer is provided, the internal default function will be used instead.
.Pp
