all return the function pointer assigned with
.Fn X509_STORE_set_check_issued ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_check_revocation ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_get_crl ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_check_crl ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_cert_crl ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_check_policy ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_lookup_certs ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_lookup_crls
and
.Fn X509_STORE_set_cleanup ,
or NULL if no assignment has been made.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_set_verify_cb_func ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_verify_func
and
.Fn X509_STORE_set_lookup_crls_cb
are aliases for
.Fn X509_STORE_set_verify_cb ,
.Fn X509_STORE_set_verify
and X509_STORE_set_lookup_crls, available as macros for backward
compatibility.
.Sh NOTES
All the callbacks from a
.Vt X509_STORE
are inherited by the corresponding
.Vt X509_STORE_CTX
structure when it is initialized.
See
.Xr X509_STORE_CTX_set_verify_cb 3
for further details.
.Sh BUGS
The macro version of this function was the only one available before
OpenSSL 1.0.0.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Xr X509_STORE_set_* 3
functions do not return a value.
.Pp
The
.Xr X509_STORE_get_* 3
functions return a pointer of the appropriate function type.
.Pp
.Fn X509_STORE_CTX_get1_issuer
returns 1 if a suitable certificate is found, 0 if not found, -1 on
other error.
